  "text": "Aeval, also spelled Eevell, Aoibheall, Aibell, Aebill or Aibhinn, was an Irish spirit. She was one of the goddesses of Ireland who survive in tale as fairy queens. Her home stood at a fairy mound near Killaloe in County Clare, in the province of Munster. A well called Tobereevul rose beneath a rock named Craganeevul. She also dwelt on the mountain Slieve Bernagh. Her name meant beautiful, but her sign foretold death. She ruled the two dozen banshees of the region. She stood at the ford as a washer, a sign of death, before the fall of the king Brian Boru. The O'Brien family kept her close. In the Midnight Court of the poet Brian Merriman she sat in judgment. Her rival, the sea fairy Clidna, changed her into a white cat.",
